From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: only the shell has <app>

Any page could create an <app> and embed any client window. The last
embed wins, so a site in a <webview> could take a window's pixels from
the shell, and window ids are sequential.

- DomicileExternalSurface is no longer stable. It is an origin trial
  feature that DomicileShell turns on for domicile://shell/ only
  (OriginTrialContext::AddFeature, in src/). Elsewhere <app> and
  <webview> are HTMLUnknownElements and their interfaces and
  canvas.embedExternalSurface() are absent.
- ExternalSurfaceProvider is a frame binder, not a process one. The
  binder refuses any frame whose origin is not domicile://shell, as the
  ControlChannel binder does.
- The embedder asks the frame's interface broker, so the canvas passes
  its frame's broker.
- <app> and <webview> set runtimeFlagHasOriginTrial, so the tokenizer
  does not read the flag without a document. Their casts match
  GetElementType(), and the HTMLFrameElementBase cast now does too: a
  <webview> outside the shell is an HTMLUnknownElement with that tag.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
